at are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 2 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+5{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 10 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ab5834f-59dc-5c91-b01d-13a6770f3977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373436} {:answer/id #uuid "a2001ebc-394f-5b1e-8e10-b391053b3f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373437} {:answer/id #uuid "4d22c7e1-baa0-5524-9ef7-e469ddd15a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17