ach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{23}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -11 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -11 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc7e00e-e3fd-5108-8329-e9833f847b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373450} {:answer/id #uuid "ee300c0c-04be-5284-9ce9-ac24b4c22bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373451} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4a495e-6289-5cb0-8c79-ac5ceaa3e69b" :answer/type {:db/ident :a