 & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -16 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & 4 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & -24 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}.$"}]}
